rota lap 4660, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; hand-advanced past rows 0-3, all read today (row 0 last at 4655, row 4 last at 4638). The threshold page and its three seats read whole. The reading turned on the Earth-Cardinal page's own claim -- a meter reads every living page for an announced ladder length and stands on the roster -- which checked out, and then on reading that meter's scratch line rather than its findings.
think Opened with the card whole, the day shelf, and the cold roster detached via standing_equipment_run.sh --detach so the transcript path was handed to me rather than typed.
think Row 4 asks for the concrete fact at the door. Took the Earth-Cardinal claim literally and checked it: announced_length stands on construction/standing-equipment.kyri at tier lap, its witness and scan both present, live reading 8 announcements all met.
think Read the scan itself rather than its output. It walks living pages into /tmp/al_found.$$ under 2>/dev/null || true and reads the file back. An absent scratch yields an empty read, and empty is a lawful answer here -- a tree announcing no ladder counts zero and passes.
think So the failure mode prints checked=0, forecasts_short=0, verdict=no_living_forecast at exit 0, and verdict=no_living_forecast is the single string the witness asserts. A guard unable to red.
think Proved it on metal before repairing: a pen holding one WIDE0-WIDE63 forecast, the same unmodified scan run twice. Writable scratch reads living_forecast and names both numbers; scratch path unwritable reads no_living_forecast at exit 0. The forecast stands in the pen either way.
think Measured the class before sweeping it. Seven tracked scans redirect a loop into scratch and read it back. Five make the file with mktemp. foundations_link_scan.sh builds its pen with mkdir -p || exit 2 and its own header already names this hazard in its own words. One did neither, so this is a repair rather than a sweep.
think Repaired with two layered checks: mktemp refusing at exit 2, and a #listing-complete sentinel written last and required back. mktemp proves the file could be created and says nothing about a write that fails partway; the sentinel is absent in that case and present in every honest one including the honest zero.
think Bit both with mutations. Removing the mktemp refusal still refused -- via the sentinel -- which is how I know the two are layered rather than redundant. Removing the sentinel check let a truncated listing print living_forecast at exit 0.
obs The script already kept the prove-before-trust discipline twice, both citing REDS %413, and skipped it on the one path that can zero the reading in silence. Preconditions are visible because the prose justifying a guard names them; plumbing is invisible for the same reason a forecast written into a name is invisible -- it reads like a fact.
obs I edited files while the cold roster pass ran, against the card's hold-still directive. The cold pass's close digest will read tree_moved; the hot pass after git add is the reading that stands for this round.
obs tracked_link went red on my own new REDS shelf, which the fold recital linked while the file was still untracked. The guard was right and staging closed it. That is the card's own clause about a lap that stops at git add, caught from the other side.
obs The other six scans carry the partial-write residue mktemp cannot see. Named rather than swept -- one sentinel each, or a shared helper, is a lap for whoever takes it.
